1.2 AirGrid Intelligence — Platform Overview
AirGrid Intelligence is the proprietary operational data and dispatch intelligence platform developed exclusively for VANTIS Air Cargo. It functions as the central integration layer connecting weather data, routing intelligence, fuel computation, cargo monitoring, FMS data feeds, and post-flight analytics into a single operational environment accessible to both dispatchers and flight crew.
AirGrid serves two primary user groups:
●	Dispatchers: Access the full AirGrid dashboard to plan routes, compute fuel loads, filter NOTAMs, review weather packages, and issue flight releases.
●	Pilots: Access a pilot-facing AirGrid view presenting the pre-flight brief, fuel summary, cargo status, active release, and real-time monitoring feeds during flight.

AirGrid is not optional. No flight operates under the VANTIS callsign without a valid, dispatcher-signed AirGrid release on file. See Section 8 for full operational usage guidance.
