Appendix E — Glossary of Terms

The following terms are used throughout this SOP. All personnel are required to be familiar with each definition.

Term / Abbreviation	Definition
AirGrid	VANTIS's proprietary Operational Intelligence Platform integrating dispatch, weather, routing, FMS data feed, cargo monitoring, and post-flight analytics. The central operational system of VANTIS Air Cargo.
ACARS	Aircraft Communications Addressing and Reporting System. The real-world digital communication system between aircraft and ground stations, replicated within VANTIS operations via Pegasus ACARS and the AirGrid Messaging Protocol (AMP).
ATC	Air Traffic Control. The authority responsible for providing separation and traffic management services to aircraft in controlled airspace, on the VATSIM network replicated by virtual controllers.
CI / Cost Index	Cost Index. A number entered into the FMC that determines the aircraft's speed schedule by balancing the relative cost of fuel burn against the cost of time. Higher CI = faster, more fuel; lower CI = slower, less fuel.
CI85	The VANTIS standard Cost Index of 85, established as the default for all Boeing 777F operations. Represents the optimal balance of fuel efficiency and trip time for long-haul cargo missions.
CRM	Crew Resource Management. The effective use of all available resources — crew, ATC, systems, AirGrid — to achieve safe and efficient flight operations.
DG / DGR	Dangerous Goods / Dangerous Goods Regulations. Hazardous materials subject to IATA DG classification, requiring special declaration, stowage, and crew notification procedures.
ETOPS	Extended-range Twin-engine Operational Performance Standards. Authorization for twin-engine aircraft to fly routes that take the aircraft beyond a specified time from a diversion airport. VANTIS holds ETOPS-180 authority.
FL	Flight Level. Altitude expressed in hundreds of feet above the international standard pressure datum (1013.25 hPa / 29.92 inHg). Example: FL380 = 38,000 ft.
FMC	Flight Management Computer. The onboard computer that manages navigation, performance, and route data. On the 777F, interfaced with the MCDU. The AirGrid AFDF feeds data directly to the FMC.
Fuel Bias P03	The VANTIS standard operational fuel buffer of +3% applied to all 777F FMS-computed block fuel figures. Designated "P03" (Plus 3%). Applied automatically by AirGrid to account for simulation fuel computation variances.
IROPS	Irregular Operations. Any unplanned event that disrupts the normal scheduled operation of a flight, including weather, technical, ATC, or network issues.
MTOW	Maximum Takeoff Weight. The maximum certified weight at which an aircraft may commence takeoff. For the 777F: 347,450 kg.
OFP	Operational Flight Plan. The complete dispatch document covering route, fuel, performance, and operational data for a specific flight. Equivalent to the AirGrid Flight Release Package in VANTIS context.
PIREP	Pilot Report. In real-world aviation: an in-flight weather report. In VANTIS context: the mandatory post-flight report submitted by the crew via AirGrid within 2 hours of block-in, covering fuel actuals, route flown, and debrief comments.
QNH	Query: Nautical Height. The altimeter setting (atmospheric pressure at sea level) that causes the altimeter to read field elevation when the aircraft is on the ground. Set by crew during descent to the destination's QNH.
QRC	Quick Reference Checklist. The abbreviated checklist used during normal and emergency operations for procedural verification. Full checklists are referenced for complete challenge-and-response sequences.
RTO	Rejected Takeoff. The deliberate abort of a takeoff roll, executed at or below V1 speed when a condition is identified requiring the takeoff to be stopped.
SELCAL	Selective Calling System. A system that allows ground stations to alert individual aircraft on HF radio by transmitting a unique 4-character tone code, avoiding continuous HF monitoring by crew. Used on oceanic tracks.
SMS	Safety Management System. A systematic, company-wide approach to managing safety, including organizational structures, accountabilities, policies, and procedures. VANTIS SMS is modeled on ICAO Doc 9859.
TOC	Top of Climb. The point in a flight at which the aircraft completes its initial climb phase and levels off at the first planned cruise altitude. A mandatory AirGrid check-in point.
TOD	Top of Descent. The point at which the aircraft commences its descent from cruise altitude toward the destination. Generated as an advisory by AirGrid. A mandatory AirGrid check-in point.
ULD	Unit Load Device. A standardized container or pallet used to consolidate individual pieces of cargo for loading into an aircraft. The 777F carries ULDs on its main deck and in lower hold positions.
VATSIM	Virtual Air Traffic Simulation Network. The global online network on which VANTIS Air Cargo conducts all virtual flight operations, providing simulated ATC and pilot-to-pilot communications.
VNT	The VANTIS Air Cargo ICAO callsign designator prefix. Used in all flight callsigns (e.g., VNT241 = VANTIS 241). Spoken as "VANTIS" followed by the flight number.
ZFW	Zero Fuel Weight. The total weight of the aircraft including all payload and crew but excluding usable fuel. Must not exceed MZFW at any point. A key W&B planning parameter.



